WEBVTT
Kind: captions

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.960 position:63%
This is the latest Apple Watch Ultra,
and even though it looks pretty similar

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:07.780 position:63%
to previous years' Apple Watches, they
quietly added some updates that made it

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:12.620 position:63%
the ultimate device for productivity,
fitness, and reducing your screen time.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.999 position:63%
It's basically three devices
in one with no compromises.

00:00:16.079 --> 00:00:18.500 position:63%
It's a full-on fitness and sleep tracker.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.520 position:63%
It's a smartphone that you can
install apps on and doesn't have any

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.880 position:63%
feeds to addict you, and it's also
a full-on productivity device.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.740 position:63%
And with this latest Apple
Watch update, I can finally say,

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:36.440 position:63%
as a Whoop user for the past
few years, I finally canceled my

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.040 position:63%
subscription and am not going
to go back to using that device.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.000 position:63%
Not only has the Apple Watch become
far more accurate than any other

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:48.860 position:63%
fitness tracker, it also has no
subscription fees and no upsells.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:52.400 position:63%
In terms of productivity, there's
even more apps that are supported now.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.220 position:63%
There's Telegram, there's WhatsApp.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:59.060 position:63%
So I can not only message
people on WhatsApp natively,

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:02.600 position:63%
I can also message my AI
assistant, and I can also respond

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.600 position:63%
to emails and finish my
to-dos directly from my watch.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.280 position:63%
The latest updates also make the
Apple Watch the ultimate dumb phone.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.680 position:63%
So you can now add on a cellular
plan for sometimes less than $5,

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:18.680 position:63%
depending on where you live, and
you can completely use almost

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:22.420 position:63%
every major feature on your iPhone
without bringing your phone out.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.040 position:63%
So you can have Apple Pay, you can have
navigation, you can use your transit

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.780 position:63%
cards, and even make phone calls
without having to bring your phone out.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.860 position:63%
So in this video, I wanna share
with you some of the latest updates,

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:37.520 position:63%
how I actually use the Apple Watch,
and why I finally replaced my

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:41.520 position:63%
other fitness trackers like the
Whoop and my Garmin with this device.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.720 position:63%
So first on the outside,
nothing looks that different.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:50.980 position:63%
It probably looks identical unless you're
looking super close up on the backside.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.520 position:63%
So right here, I have last
year's Apple Watch Ultra,

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.680 position:63%
and this is this year's Apple
Watch Ultra, and as you can see,

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.580 position:63%
it looks literally exactly the same
except for the sensors on the back.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:05.500 position:63%
But these sensors are actually a
massive upgrade to the Apple Watch.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:10.080 position:63%
So they basically put in a completely new
set of optical and electrical sensors.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:13.220 position:63%
So now it measures your
heart rate every five seconds

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:17.320 position:63%
instead of every five minutes,
which is a massive upgrade.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.220 position:63%
So they were able to do that without
sacrificing the battery life at all.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.400 position:63%
This is probably one of the
biggest edges that other fitness

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:27.620 position:63%
trackers had like Garmin or
the Whoop for many years.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:31.520 position:63%
But now along with this, along with
heart rate variability tracking, it's

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:36.640 position:63%
pretty much on par or even better than
any other fitness tracker on the market.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:40.240 position:63%
They also added some pretty simple but
major quality of life improvements.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.180 position:63%
For example, now you
can see your heart rate

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:46.100 position:63%
and your daily steps
directly on the watch face.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:47.980 position:63%
This was previously not possible.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.600 position:63%
I don't know why it took them so long to
implement this, but now you can see your

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:56.320 position:63%
live heart rate and your live step count,
which is, pretty nice and convenient.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:02.080 position:63%
So this upgraded sensor, along with
the completely redesigned health app,

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.580 position:63%
has made me completely
quit using the Whoop.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:08.060 position:63%
So prior to this, I was a pretty
loyal Whoop user for three years.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.080 position:63%
But even though I used it for
three years and I was paying

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:14.020 position:63%
the subscription, I never really
enjoyed using the Whoop app.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.760 position:63%
Like I, I didn't really
enjoy the Whoop experience.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.680 position:63%
They constantly had different upsells,

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.460 position:63%
and if you upgrade the device,
you have to buy new accessories.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:24.720 position:63%
Yeah, most of the people that I know that
use Whoop also had a similar experience,

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:28.280 position:63%
like the app itself is not
that easy or intuitive to use.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:30.580 position:63%
It was more that Whoop
just filled this super

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.640 position:63%
niche space in the market
that nobody else could.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:37.540 position:63%
But now Apple has almost full feature
parity with the major features that people

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:42.000 position:63%
enjoyed on Whoop, and it's way easier
to use in the newly designed health app.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.640 position:63%
So for example, now you have a dashboard
that you can see your activity,

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:51.880 position:63%
you can see your sleep score, your vitals
and heart rate variability, and I find

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:55.960 position:63%
it personally to be way better designed
and way easier to use than the Whoop app.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:59.340 position:63%
And it just feels good to know
that I'm not unnecessarily paying

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:02.020 position:63%
a subscription for something that
shouldn't cost a subscription.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:05.020 position:63%
Like, all the things that are happening on

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.020 position:63%
the Whoop app should
not cost a subscription.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.800 position:63%
It doesn't cost them anything to
calculate any of those things.

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:13.060 position:63%
So I really enjoy this new
health app and being able to

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:17.379 position:63%
see just as detailed insights
into my sleep and into my

00:04:17.459 --> 00:04:20.960 position:63%
workouts as I did before
with other fitness trackers.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:25.060 position:63%
And I would argue that if you care
about your health and fitness tracking,

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:29.380 position:63%
the Apple Watch Ultra or even
just the regular Apple Watch is

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:32.800 position:63%
unparalleled with any other fitness
tracker on the market because

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:36.840 position:63%
it has a lot of other features
like ECG, blood oxygen tracking.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.560 position:63%
It can detect sleep apnea,
and there are things

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.340 position:63%
that could genuinely
help you save your life.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.920 position:63%
Like, you can call emergency
services with one click,

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:49.280 position:63%
and it could generate a super loud siren
if you're lost or trapped somewhere,

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:52.500 position:63%
and it can even notice you if
you have irregular heartbeats.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:56.720 position:63%
I personally know somebody
that was able to get something

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:00.720 position:63%
life-saving diagnosed because
of wearing an Apple Watch.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.900 position:63%
So I don't think that's
something that you can really

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:05.520 position:63%
get with any other wearable
on the market right now.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:09.120 position:63%
There's also this guy called The
Quantified Scientist on YouTube

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:13.960 position:63%
that he tests all fitness trackers
scientifically and compares them,

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.120 position:63%
and the Apple Watch is consistently
one of the most accurate ones,

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:20.560 position:63%
even beating Whoop and
Oura in some of his tests.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:23.880 position:63%
So honestly, in my opinion, there's
no reason to get a Whoop anymore.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:25.620 position:63%
I could see an argument for, like,

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:28.680 position:63%
a wearable ring because the form
factor is completely different.

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:31.700 position:63%
But if you're considering getting a
Whoop or any other fitness tracker,

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:34.960 position:63%
I think the Apple Watch is
literally going to be the best one.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:39.680 position:63%
Another thing that they improved with the
Apple Watch this year is the battery life.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:43.380 position:63%
So not only is the battery life
way longer on the Ultra with

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:46.180 position:63%
up to 48 hours, but you can
also charge it super quickly.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:50.040 position:63%
So in 15 minutes, you can
get up to 12 hours of charge.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:53.240 position:63%
So for me, I just charge it
when I'm taking a shower,

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:56.520 position:63%
and that's been enough for me to
use for basically the whole day.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:59.360 position:63%
The battery life is also long
enough now to run ultra marathons,

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:02.700 position:63%
which is, a pretty major upgrade
because, like, two years ago,

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:05.360 position:63%
I ran a marathon with just
a regular Apple Watch,

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:09.952 position:63%
and it barely made it past four
hours with constant tracking.

00:06:10.112 --> 00:06:14.032 position:63%
So it's good to know that now it
can pretty much track any marathon.

00:06:14.112 --> 00:06:18.692 position:63%
One underrated tip that I haven't seen
anyone talk about is if you turn on low

00:06:18.772 --> 00:06:23.512 position:63%
power mode on the Apple Watch Ultra, you
can basically double your battery life.

00:06:23.592 --> 00:06:27.272 position:63%
So with the Apple Watch Ultra, if you
turn on low power mode and you are

00:06:27.352 --> 00:06:32.512 position:63%
not tracking your workouts, you can use
it for up to five days battery life.

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:34.912 position:63%
And personally, I think that's
pretty insane because this

00:06:34.992 --> 00:06:38.432 position:63%
isn't just a fitness tracker,
it's also a productivity device.

00:06:38.512 --> 00:06:41.092 position:63%
It's also a modern dumb phone.

00:06:41.872 --> 00:06:43.952 position:63%
And that leads me to the
next part of this video,

00:06:44.032 --> 00:06:46.632 position:63%
which is to use it as
a productivity device.

00:06:46.752 --> 00:06:48.612 position:63%
Obviously, if you wanted
to, you could turn off all

00:06:48.692 --> 00:06:52.572 position:63%
notifications and just use it
as a dedicated fitness tracker.

00:06:52.832 --> 00:06:55.832 position:63%
But I also find it really
useful to install some of my

00:06:55.912 --> 00:06:59.092 position:63%
most used productivity apps
so that I can access them.

00:06:59.172 --> 00:07:03.992 position:63%
So, like my to-do app, Things 3,
Notes, and even Telegram and WhatsApp.

00:07:04.072 --> 00:07:05.632 position:63%
There are even apps that
you can install that can

00:07:05.712 --> 00:07:08.812 position:63%
help you take meeting notes
in real life autonomously.

00:07:08.892 --> 00:07:11.652 position:63%
So if you're going for a
doctor visit or you're having

00:07:11.732 --> 00:07:13.592 position:63%
a meeting in real life and
you don't have your computer,

00:07:13.712 --> 00:07:16.412 position:63%
you can still have your Apple
Watch take notes for you.

00:07:16.652 --> 00:07:19.832 position:63%
And that's where the sponsor of
this video comes in, Granola.

00:07:19.912 --> 00:07:21.732 position:63%
So Granola is an app that automatically

00:07:21.812 --> 00:07:24.252 position:63%
takes notes from any
meeting that you're in.

00:07:24.332 --> 00:07:28.832 position:63%
The main app is on your laptop, and how
it works is that it detects when you're in

00:07:28.912 --> 00:07:33.872 position:63%
a call, takes notes quietly, and then just
shows you the summary when you're done.

00:07:33.952 --> 00:07:37.092 position:63%
Once you set it up, it works
super seamlessly, and it has saved

00:07:37.172 --> 00:07:39.892 position:63%
me a bunch of times when I forgot
to take notes in a meeting.

00:07:39.972 --> 00:07:45.072 position:63%
What's cool about Granola is that it works
in any meeting platform app that you use.

00:07:45.152 --> 00:07:50.332 position:63%
So whether that's Discord or Google
Meets or Zoom, it automatically

00:07:50.412 --> 00:07:53.292 position:63%
will be able to get the audio and
transcribe it and give you a summary.

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:56.352 position:63%
And unlike other apps
that do something similar,

00:07:56.432 --> 00:08:00.152 position:63%
it doesn't have a bot that joins the
call, which gives pressure to everyone.

00:08:00.232 --> 00:08:03.152 position:63%
They also have a dedicated
app for the Apple Watch,

00:08:03.232 --> 00:08:05.072 position:63%
and it works just as seamlessly.

00:08:05.152 --> 00:08:08.112 position:63%
So I have it on my watch face,
and all I have to do is tap on it,

00:08:08.192 --> 00:08:12.112 position:63%
click start, and it will take
notes and transcribe the meeting

00:08:12.192 --> 00:08:15.752 position:63%
without me having to pull out
my computer or do anything else.

00:08:15.832 --> 00:08:18.112 position:63%
It can even transcribe
other languages and give

00:08:18.192 --> 00:08:20.652 position:63%
you the summary in the
language of your choice.

00:08:20.792 --> 00:08:25.232 position:63%
So that has also come in
handy for me before in Japan.

00:08:25.312 --> 00:08:27.932 position:63%
For me, this single app has really
helped me have less pressure when

00:08:28.012 --> 00:08:31.692 position:63%
it comes to meetings, and also
helped me stay more present in the

00:08:31.772 --> 00:08:35.192 position:63%
meeting itself because I don't
have to be focused on taking notes.

00:08:35.312 --> 00:08:38.012 position:63%
You can try it for free with
the link in the description.

00:08:38.092 --> 00:08:41.172 position:63%
The basic plan is completely
free, and it covers more than

00:08:41.252 --> 00:08:44.652 position:63%
enough for most people's needs
with unlimited transcriptions.

00:08:44.732 --> 00:08:46.552 position:63%
But yeah, let's get back into the video.

00:08:47.292 --> 00:08:50.552 position:63%
So along with that app, the most
used productivity apps that I use

00:08:50.632 --> 00:08:56.112 position:63%
on my Apple Watch is first my to-do
app, Things 3, and also Telegram.

00:08:56.192 --> 00:08:59.892 position:63%
The app Things 3 has been my go-to
to-do app for many years now,

00:09:00.252 --> 00:09:05.292 position:63%
and on the Apple Watch, it syncs
seamlessly with all my devices instantly.

00:09:05.372 --> 00:09:08.292 position:63%
So I can add a new to-do
just with my voice.

00:09:08.372 --> 00:09:09.392 position:63%
I can complete them.

00:09:09.772 --> 00:09:13.652 position:63%
And yeah, it just works without any
subscriptions and any other setup.

00:09:13.732 --> 00:09:17.612 position:63%
With this to-do app, there are widgets
that you can add to your watch face

00:09:17.692 --> 00:09:20.512 position:63%
or in the control center, so I can
easily see the things that I have to do.

00:09:20.592 --> 00:09:23.752 position:63%
But another app that I
also use a lot is Telegram.

00:09:23.832 --> 00:09:26.812 position:63%
Telegram has become
super useful and maybe my

00:09:26.952 --> 00:09:30.672 position:63%
most used app since I
set up my AI assistant.

00:09:30.752 --> 00:09:32.052 position:63%
So if you haven't seen the last video,

00:09:32.132 --> 00:09:36.492 position:63%
I basically set up a AI
assistant on my old MacBook Air,

00:09:36.632 --> 00:09:41.092 position:63%
and it can control the computer and
basically do any task that I need it to.

00:09:41.172 --> 00:09:43.152 position:63%
So it runs behind a frontier model,

00:09:43.452 --> 00:09:47.052 position:63%
and I can actually have it do
things like control my computer.

00:09:47.132 --> 00:09:49.132 position:63%
I can get really detailed
responses for questions

00:09:49.212 --> 00:09:51.972 position:63%
that I have and actually get tasks done.

00:09:52.052 --> 00:09:56.072 position:63%
Like, I can have it write a draft
based on a voice memo that I send,

00:09:56.152 --> 00:09:59.072 position:63%
or it can even help me
purchase movie tickets.

00:09:59.152 --> 00:10:03.972 position:63%
I can actually purchase movie tickets from
my Apple Watch, which is pretty insane.

00:10:04.052 --> 00:10:07.392 position:63%
This was not possible last year
or even maybe six months ago.

00:10:07.472 --> 00:10:11.492 position:63%
If you use Claude Code or
any agentic coding setup,

00:10:11.892 --> 00:10:13.772 position:63%
I would also recommend
the app called Moshi.

00:10:13.852 --> 00:10:17.692 position:63%
Like, they have a iPhone app, and
they also have an Apple Watch app.

00:10:17.772 --> 00:10:20.312 position:63%
So you can use this app
to check on your agents.

00:10:20.392 --> 00:10:23.932 position:63%
You can approve different
tasks, directly from the watch.

00:10:24.012 --> 00:10:25.192 position:63%
So I think it's pretty cool.

00:10:25.272 --> 00:10:28.132 position:63%
The only thing I wish I could do
that I haven't found a good way to do

00:10:28.212 --> 00:10:33.192 position:63%
yet is to map the action button to
send a voice memo to my AI assistant.

00:10:33.272 --> 00:10:37.632 position:63%
Like, that seems doable, but I haven't
found a good way to have that set up yet.

00:10:37.892 --> 00:10:42.592 position:63%
You can access Siri pretty easily just
by holding on the dial, but for me,

00:10:42.672 --> 00:10:46.412 position:63%
it hasn't been really that useful,
even though it's improved a lot,

00:10:46.712 --> 00:10:52.712 position:63%
especially since I have had a taste
of Hermes and using a frontier model.

00:10:52.972 --> 00:10:56.552 position:63%
But yeah, with this Telegram chat,
I can literally track my macros.

00:10:56.632 --> 00:10:58.352 position:63%
I can add stuff to my calendar.

00:10:58.572 --> 00:11:01.432 position:63%
I can check on YouTube
analytics and even order

00:11:01.512 --> 00:11:04.012 position:63%
Uber Eats without needing my phone at all.

00:11:04.092 --> 00:11:06.732 position:63%
If you're interested in that setup,
you can check out my previous video.

00:11:06.812 --> 00:11:08.692 position:63%
I think what's also really powerful now,

00:11:08.952 --> 00:11:12.432 position:63%
because we have so many frontier
models and they're way cheaper to use,

00:11:12.512 --> 00:11:17.112 position:63%
is that you can even make custom
productivity apps or custom apps on your

00:11:17.192 --> 00:11:22.612 position:63%
Apple Watch just for yourself, like,
just for a very specific niche use case,

00:11:22.752 --> 00:11:25.332 position:63%
and that hasn't really been
possible up until right now.

00:11:25.412 --> 00:11:28.132 position:63%
So yeah, I think the
possibilities are endless,

00:11:28.292 --> 00:11:31.992 position:63%
and that's what makes the Apple
Watch so powerful because you can't

00:11:32.072 --> 00:11:36.492 position:63%
really do that on other fitness
trackers or other smartwatches.

00:11:37.092 --> 00:11:40.972 position:63%
Which leads me to the third
thing that makes the Apple Watch

00:11:41.152 --> 00:11:45.632 position:63%
so powerful is that it is also
the ultimate device that helps

00:11:45.712 --> 00:11:48.492 position:63%
you reduce your screen time
by replacing your smartphone.

00:11:48.572 --> 00:11:50.832 position:63%
You still need a smartphone
to actually set this up,

00:11:50.912 --> 00:11:54.792 position:63%
but with the latest Apple
Watch, you no longer have to be

00:11:54.872 --> 00:11:58.672 position:63%
chained to your smartphone and
bring them out wherever you go.

00:11:58.792 --> 00:12:01.012 position:63%
In most countries, you
can get a Apple Watch

00:12:01.092 --> 00:12:04.192 position:63%
cellular plan added on for less than $10.

00:12:04.272 --> 00:12:05.952 position:63%
In Japan, it's less than $5.

00:12:06.032 --> 00:12:10.932 position:63%
And it's actually extremely underrated
to have this set up because now

00:12:11.312 --> 00:12:14.680 position:63%
I don't have to bring my phone out,
and I'm not required to bring my

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:19.060 position:63%
phone out whenever I go anywhere, so
it's more of a conscious decision.

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:20.780 position:63%
I can still message people pretty easily.

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:21.800 position:63%
There's iMessage.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:25.340 position:63%
There are also native Telegram
and WhatsApp apps now.

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:28.640 position:63%
There's also a complete, feature
complete Apple Maps, so I can get

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:33.540 position:63%
directions walking to anywhere or
even get transit directions, and even

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:39.880 position:63%
be able to tap in at the metro
with the Apple Pay, on my watch.

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:42.160 position:63%
Yeah, personally, I find it to
be way more ergonomic to look at

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:45.580 position:63%
directions directly on my wrist,
because it's just right there,

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:48.280 position:63%
and it also will vibrate
if I have to make a turn.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:53.900 position:63%
And I can also listen to audiobooks and
music directly from the Apple Watch.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:58.120 position:63%
Like, I can play it out loud, or it
connects to any Bluetooth headphones.

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:00.160 position:63%
I think what's really nice about
having a dumb phone on your

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:04.020 position:63%
wrist is that it's really the
ultimate utilitarian device.

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:05.740 position:63%
You physically cannot doom scroll on it.

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:08.080 position:63%
There are basically no
apps that have feeds,

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:10.660 position:63%
and it's also really
hard to physically do.

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:14.040 position:63%
It just gives you more freedom to
not have to be chained to your phone.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:17.440 position:63%
Like, I can just bring my e-reader
and go out for the whole day,

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:19.820 position:63%
or just bring a book and
go out for the whole day.

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:23.220 position:63%
The Wallet app and Apple Pay
is also super underrated,

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:26.700 position:63%
and it's not really present
in any other fitness tracker

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:30.380 position:63%
or really smartwatch, even
though they sort of have it.

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:32.900 position:63%
It's just super seamless
to use on the Apple Watch.

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:36.820 position:63%
I can tap in, for transit cards,

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:40.000 position:63%
and I can also access all of
my credit cards really easily.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:43.740 position:63%
I even have my Anytime Fitness gym card,
directly on my Apple Watch, so I can tap

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:49.620 position:63%
into the gym, and you can have plane
tickets, even a digital passport.

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:52.760 position:63%
I'm not sure if you can actually
use that yet, but, I have that.

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:56.460 position:63%
So yeah, it's really uncomparable
to anything on the market right now.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:59.680 position:63%
But with all that being said, there
are still a few caveats with the Apple

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:03.560 position:63%
Watch if you're considering getting one
that you should probably know first.

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:07.120 position:63%
And I'll say first, the main
downside with the Apple Watch is that

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:11.440 position:63%
compared to other fitness trackers,
it can be a little bit bulky because,

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:15.160 position:63%
you know, they have so much
crammed into this singular device.

00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:19.500 position:63%
Like, going from sleeping with an Oura
Ring or a Whoop to the Apple Watch Ultra,

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:24.320 position:63%
it's definitely a lot bulkier, especially
with the edges being, like, quite sharp.

00:14:24.560 --> 00:14:28.060 position:63%
But after, like, a week of
doing it, I got used to it,

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:30.940 position:63%
and now I don't really feel that
at all, and I feel kind of weird

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:34.860 position:63%
and exposed when I don't have my
Apple Watch when I'm sleeping.

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:36.640 position:63%
I also like using the
alarm on the Apple Watch.

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:40.040 position:63%
I find it to be less,
intrusive or less, like,

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:43.580 position:63%
jarring than, than having,
like, a phone alarm.

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:45.400 position:63%
The second thing that I find to be kind of

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:48.420 position:63%
hard to use is the
built-in Apple Watch cable.

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:51.420 position:63%
So, once you get the Apple Watch,
you it comes with this, like,

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:56.640 position:63%
cable with a USB-C on the end and, like,
this puck that you put the Apple Watch on.

00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:58.640 position:63%
And I find that to be pretty hard to use.

00:14:58.720 --> 00:15:01.900 position:63%
Like, there are times when I put my
Apple Watch on that, and I place it on

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:05.960 position:63%
the table, and then it kind of, like,
misaligns, so it ends up not charging.

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:08.760 position:63%
And I just think it's kind of
awkward and not that stable.

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:11.540 position:63%
So I would recommend getting a
third-party Apple Watch charger.

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:16.220 position:63%
For example, I got this one that is
in my bathroom next to my shower,

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:20.260 position:63%
so when I go shower, I can just place
it on here, and it's super stable.

00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:22.000 position:63%
I can see how much it's charging,

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:24.800 position:63%
and I don't have to fiddle
with any cables or any wires.

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:27.220 position:63%
But either way, I think compared
to other fitness trackers,

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:29.820 position:63%
it's still way better because,
like, when I had a Garmin,

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:33.240 position:63%
I had to get this adapter that
would plug into a USB-C or,

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:35.000 position:63%
or else I had to bring
this, like, special cable.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:37.180 position:63%
There was one time that
I was in another country,

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:41.140 position:63%
and I lost my Garmin charger
and had to go find a dedicated

00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:45.300 position:63%
Garmin store just to get the
charger, which was pretty difficult.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:48.720 position:63%
But with Apple Watches, because
so many people use them,

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:53.820 position:63%
it's really easy to find a accessory or
additional charger for the Apple Watch.

00:15:54.020 --> 00:15:59.220 position:63%
Like, there are, battery banks with an
Apple Watch charger built in, and you

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:04.720 position:63%
can even get them, I, I think, at 7-Eleven
like a convenience store in Japan.

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:07.540 position:63%
But all in all, I think those
are some pretty minor downsides

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:11.640 position:63%
compared to the major benefits
that you get with the Apple Watch.

00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:13.940 position:63%
Like, it could literally save your life.

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:18.460 position:63%
It's one of the best modern dumb
phones that you can get today,

00:16:18.900 --> 00:16:23.420 position:63%
and there's even some more powerful stuff
that's coming in updates later this year.

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:26.920 position:63%
And if you are like me and used a Whoop,
you're literally going to save more money

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:30.620 position:63%
in the long run because you don't need
to pay a subscription to Whoop anymore.

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:32.240 position:63%
But yeah, that's it for this video.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:33.320 position:63%
I'll see you in the next one.

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:34.400 position:63%
Let's get it.

